---
layout: base.njk
title: "Modules & Instruments"
description: "Complete reference of Perception's built-in physical instruments, 36+ modular DSP components, grain clouds, formula melodies, and isolated VST3 workers."
---

<section class="section grid-backdrop">
  <div class="shell">
    <div class="section-head">
      <p class="eyebrow"><span class="dot dot-signal" aria-hidden="true"></span>Modular DSP &amp; Built-In Voices</p>
      <h1>Instruments &amp; 36+ Signal Modules</h1>
      <p>
        Start with a physical waveguide string, bowed string, bell, mallet, or phase-distortion
        operator — or patch custom per-note graphs from 36+ typed DSP components and isolated VST3 plug-ins.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="filter-bar" role="group" aria-label="Filter instruments by category">
      <button type="button" class="filter-btn" data-filter="all" aria-pressed="true">All instruments</button>
      <button type="button" class="filter-btn" data-filter="modular" aria-pressed="false">Modular</button>
      <button type="button" class="filter-btn" data-filter="physical" aria-pressed="false">Physical</button>
      <button type="button" class="filter-btn" data-filter="synth" aria-pressed="false">Synthesis</button>
      <button type="button" class="filter-btn" data-filter="percussion" aria-pressed="false">Percussion</button>
    </div>

    <div class="card-grid">
      {% for inst in site.instruments %}
      <article class="card" data-category="{{ inst.category }}">
        <span class="card-tag{% if inst.category == 'physical' %} is-monitor{% elif inst.category == 'modular' %} is-mod{% endif %}">{{ inst.category }}</span>
        <h3 class="mono">{{ inst.kind }}</h3>
        <p>{{ inst.summary }}</p>
        <p class="mono" style="font-size:0.78rem; color: var(--ink);">{{ inst.controls }}</p>
      </article>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="shell">
    <div class="section-head">
      <p class="eyebrow"><span class="dot dot-mod" aria-hidden="true"></span>Patch Graph Library</p>
      <h2>Typed DSP Components</h2>
      <p>
        Perception validates port rates, units, channel counts, and feedback cycles on every cable.
        Invalid connections leave the previous graph intact; Undo restores deleted nodes and cables together.
      </p>
    </div>

    {% for group in site.moduleGroups %}
    <div class="module-group">
      <h3>
        <span class="dot dot-{{ group.accent }}" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        {{ group.name }}
      </h3>
      <ul class="chip-list">
        {% for item in group.items %}
        <li class="chip">{{ item }}</li>
        {% endfor %}
      </ul>
    </div>
    {% endfor %}

    <div class="card-grid" style="margin-top:28px">
      <article class="card">
        <span class="card-tag">Grain Cloud</span>
        <h3>16-Voice Granular Synthesis</h3>
        <p>
          Load little-endian RIFF/WAVE files up to 8 MiB (8–192 kHz, 8/16/24/32-bit PCM or float32).
          Control source position, playback rate (zero holds, negative reverses), grain duration,
          pan, onset interval, and jitter — with full sample undo history.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <span class="card-tag is-mod">Formula Melodies</span>
        <h3>Deterministic Step Expressions</h3>
        <p>
          Type a formula over step <code class="mono">t</code> — such as
          <code class="mono">60 + t * 7 % 12</code> — and <code class="mono">formulaNotes</code>
          emits one MIDI note per step straight into oscillators, delays, or VST3 instruments.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <span class="card-tag is-monitor">Isolated VST3 Workers</span>
        <h3>Sandboxed Plug-In Execution</h3>
        <p>
          Point Settings at your VST3 folder. Each discovered instrument or effect runs in its own
          separate worker process with sample-positioned MIDI, parameter automation, and state restore.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
